# Identity

Replace this with your own identity. This file lives in `always/`, so it is
re-injected into every session — keep it to the handful of facts worth that
cost, and stay well under 1 KB (the whole `always/` directory has a hard 8 KB
budget shared across all files).

Good things to put here: who you are, your role/team, and the primary
technologies or domain you work in. Anything more situational (per-project
facts, task rules, reasoning) belongs in `topics/`, `when/`, or `knowledge/` —
see `knowledge/anatomy-of-good-memory.md`.

Example (delete and replace):

> I'm a backend engineer on the payments team. I work mostly in Python and Go,
> and I own the billing service.
